(TICKET TO RIDE - Demo Rulebook \(Board Game Cafe\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OVERVIEW) Tj T*
(Players build train routes across a map of North America. You score points for claimed) Tj T*
(routes, for completed destination tickets and for the longest continuous railway.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(COMPONENTS) Tj T*
(45 trains per player, 110 train cards \(12 of each of 8 colors plus 14 locomotives\) and) Tj T*
(destination tickets.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SETUP) Tj T*
(Each player gets 4 train cards. Turn 5 train cards face up next to the deck. Each) Tj T*
(player draws 3 destination tickets and must keep at least 2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(YOUR TURN) Tj T*
(On your turn you do exactly one of these three actions:) Tj T*
(1. Draw train cards: take 2 cards, face up or from the deck. If you take a face-up) Tj T*
(   locomotive,) Tj T*
(   it is your only card for the turn. You may not take a face-up locomotive as your) Tj T*
(   second card.) Tj T*
(2. Claim a route: play as many cards of the route's color as the route has spaces,) Tj T*
(   then put) Tj T*
(   your trains on it. Gray routes can be claimed with cards of any single color.) Tj T*
(   Locomotives) Tj T*
(   are wild and replace any color.) Tj T*
(3. Draw destination tickets: draw 3 tickets and keep at least 1.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If three locomotives are face up at the same time, discard all five cards and turn up) Tj T*
(five new.) Tj T*
ET
