(DOUBLE ROUTES) Tj T*
(Some cities are linked by two parallel routes. One player may not claim both. In games) Tj T*
(with 2 or 3 players only one of the two routes can be used.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ROUTE SCORING) Tj T*
(Route length 1: 1 point. 2: 2 points. 3: 4 points. 4: 7 points. 5: 10 points. 6: 15) Tj T*
(points. Points are scored immediately when the route is claimed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(END OF THE GAME) Tj T*
(When a player has 2 or fewer trains left at the end of their turn, every player,) Tj T*
(including that player, gets one final turn.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FINAL SCORING) Tj T*
(- Each completed destination ticket adds its value; each incomplete ticket subtracts) Tj T*
(   its value.) Tj T*
(- The player with the longest continuous path of trains gets a 10-point bonus.) Tj T*
(The player with the most points wins. On a tie, the player with the most completed) Tj T*
(tickets wins.) Tj T*
ET
